  "topics": [
    {
      "body": [
        "A **preset** is one complete look; each preset becomes one choice in the game's eye makeup selector. A preset is built from **layers**, which stack like real makeup: the top of the Layers list sits in front.",
        "",
        "- Add, duplicate, hide and remove layers from the Layers panel.",
        "- Drag a row's grip, or use [[key:rows.reorder]], to change the order.",
        "- [[key:rows.rename]] renames the focused row.",
      ],
      "id": "layers",
      "keywords": "layer stack order preset look collection selector front",
      "title": "Layers and presets",
      "tours": [
        "onboarding",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "Shape the selected layer on the **UV map** or directly on the head.",
        "",
        "- Drag a point to reshape the outline; drag inside the shape to move it.",
        "- Double-click the outline in the UV map to add a point.",
        "- Hold **Shift** and drag to rotate the shape, or Shift-wheel to scale it.",
        "- Esc cancels a drag while you're still holding it.",
        "",
        "The Shape, Pigment & edge and Warp panels hold the finer controls.",
      ],
      "id": "drawing",
      "keywords": "draw uv map point curve bezier shape move rotate scale warp soft edge",
      "title": "Drawing and shaping",
      "tours": [
        "onboarding",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "The head shows your makeup on V. Drag off the makeup to turn the view, use the wheel to zoom and right-drag to pan; [[key:head.front]] returns to the front view.",
        "",
        "The 3D view is built from your own Cyberpunk 2077 files the first time. If it isn't ready, the head pane shows the one next step. The UV map, library and Check all work without it.",
      ],
      "id": "head",
      "keywords": "head 3d preview camera orbit zoom pan front view wolvenkit setup",
      "title": "The 3D view",
    },
    {
      "body": "Each layer has a colour, an opacity and a finish. **Matte**, **Satin** and **Metallic** can go into your mod. **Glossy** and **Colour-shifting** can be built as experiments. **Shimmer** and **Glitter** are being reworked and wait for a check in the game, so the picker shows them only with **Show research tools** on (Settings › Appearance). A layer that already uses one keeps it.",
      "id": "finishes",
      "keywords": "colour color finish matte satin metallic shimmer glossy glitter colour-shift duochrome export preview only",
      "title": "Colours and finishes",
      "tours": [
        "onboarding",
        "whats-new-0.1.0-beta.1",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": "Every change can be undone. [[key:shell.undo]] undoes, and [[key:shell.redo]] redoes. Undo follows what you last edited: a preset or a V. View and lighting changes have their own Undo. The **History** panel names what you last edited and lists your recent changes to it; click any step to go back to it.",
      "id": "undo",
      "keywords": "undo redo history back step mistake",
      "title": "Undo, Redo and History",
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "Your work saves itself to your local library as you go. **Save version** ([[key:shell.save]]) keeps a version of your collection there, beside its earlier versions, that you can go back to.",
        "",
        "Opening or importing another collection never replaces the one you had open: it stays in your library, and **Reopen previous** shows it again. Collections never saved as a version are listed under **Recent drafts** in the Library panel, where **Reopen** shows one.",
        "",
        "To keep a separate copy or share looks, export the collection as a file from the Library panel, and import it again on any computer.",
      ],
      "id": "library",
      "keywords": "save library version autosave draft export import backup share file",
      "title": "Saving and your library",
      "tours": [
        "onboarding",
        "whats-new-0.1.0-beta.1",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "Open **Mod package** when your looks are ready.",
        "",
        "- **Check** lists which presets and layers can become mod files, and names anything that would be left out and why. It needs no game files.",
        "- **Build** makes your own **XF Eye Artistry** mod files. Nothing goes into your game until you add it: see **Installing your mod**.",
      ],
      "id": "package",
      "keywords": "mod package check build xf eye artistry archive install game",
      "title": "Making your mod: Check and Build",
      "tours": [
        "onboarding",
        "first-eye-mod",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "After **Build**, each mod in the result has two buttons.",
        "",
        "- **Add to my mod manager** shows exactly what would be added and where before anything changes: with Mod Organizer 2, the mod's own folder and one new row in your profile's mod list, at the bottom of the lowest section that doesn't hold frameworks (your separators and every other mod stay where they are). Without Mod Organizer 2, its files go into the game folder: archive\\pc\\mod, and r6\\tweaks for a mod that has TweakXL files. Choose **Add** to go ahead.",
        "- **Show in folder** opens the built mod, to install it by hand: copy its **archive** folder (and its **r6** folder, when it has one) into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder, or add it to Vortex as a mod.",
        "",
        "XF Studio never replaces files it didn't put there, never changes your frameworks or other mods, and waits while Mod Organizer 2 is open (it rewrites its mod list when it closes). Adding a newer build replaces only the files it added before. If the eye makeup row is missing, check that **XF Eye Artistry** is switched on in your mod manager. Launch the game through Mod Organizer 2 if you use it. Open **Settings › Game › Mod frameworks**: it shows which **ArchiveXL**, **RED4ext** and **redscript** the game will load, says if one is too old or missing, and links to its latest release on Nexus Mods and GitHub. XF Studio never installs or updates frameworks for you. If something still looks wrong, **Report a problem…** in Help prepares a report for you to review.",
        "",
        "Your game folder and mod manager are chosen in **Settings › Game** (the Settings button at the top right), and **Settings › Game › Mod frameworks** shows whether the frameworks your mod needs are in place.",
      ],
      "id": "install",
      "keywords": "install add mod manager mo2 mod organizer vortex game folder archive show in folder profile modlist separator framework frameworks archivexl red4ext redscript update version",
      "title": "Installing your mod",
      "tours": [
        "first-eye-mod",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "Everything XF Studio needs to know about your computer is in **Settings**: the Settings button at the top right, or type “Settings” in the command palette ([[key:shell.palette]]).",
        "",
        "- **Game**: your Cyberpunk 2077 folder and how you install mods (Mod Organizer 2 and its profile, or Vortex and the game folder). XF Studio finds these for you, and under **Mod frameworks** shows whether the frameworks your mod needs (ArchiveXL, RED4ext and redscript) are in place.",
        "- **Saves**: where your saves are. XF Studio uses the game's own folder, Saved Games\\CD Projekt Red\\Cyberpunk 2077; choose another if you keep them somewhere else.",
        "- **Tools**: WolvenKit, which XF Studio sets up for you.",
        "- **Appearance**, and **Privacy & diagnostics**.",
        "",
        "Each choice is saved on this computer as you make it.",
      ],
      "id": "settings",
      "keywords": "settings preferences options configure where game folder mod manager mo2 mod organizer vortex profile saves folder saved games save explorer wolvenkit theme appearance diagnostics privacy framework frameworks archivexl red4ext redscript",
      "title": "Settings: your game, saves and tools",
      "tours": [
        "your-v-and-view",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "Load a save from the **Character** panel and the 3D view shows that V's own skin, makeup and face details, eyes, brows, lashes, hair, piercings and body, read from your game and mods. Your looks and library are never changed by loading a save.",
        "",
        "You can change any creator option there too, to check your looks on another face, and save a set of options as a preset to use again. None of this changes the save itself.",
      ],
      "id": "character",
      "keywords": "save v character brows lashes hair eye shape load",
      "title": "Your V in the 3D view",
      "tours": [
        "your-v-and-view",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "**Camera & light** frames the 3D view and lights your V.",
        "",
        "- **Camera**: the front view ([[key:head.front]]), the whole body, the character creator's own face and hair cameras, and the field of view.",
        "- **Light**: choose a lighting setup. **Character creator** uses the game's own creator lights, to compare with what you see in the game. Make a new setup to change its lights, their colour and their direction on the dial.",
        "",
        "Camera and light are saved with your workspace. They never change your looks or your mod.",
      ],
      "id": "camera",
      "keywords": "camera light lighting setup creator studio exposure backdrop grade field of view front view whole body lens direction dial",
      "title": "Camera & light",
      "tours": [
        "your-v-and-view",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "When something goes wrong, the notice shows a reference such as **XF-7K3Q** and a **Report this problem** button. You can also report from here, or from the command palette.",
        "",
        "- The report is prepared for you to review first. Nothing leaves your computer unless you send it.",
        "- Include each part or turn it off. Personal folder names and e-mail addresses are already replaced.",
        "- **Save report** makes one file to attach to a GitHub issue; **Open a GitHub issue** starts one for you.",
        "- XF Studio keeps the last half hour of what it worked out (which mod supplied what), so you don't have to make the problem happen again. **Diagnostic mode** keeps more, for a day.",
        "",
        "Your mods are identified by name, version and download source, never copied. Reports on GitHub are **public**: only include a mod's own files if you made it, or its permissions allow sharing it.",
      ],
      "id": "report",
      "keywords": "bug error problem report issue github log diagnostics crash reference mod files privacy",
      "title": "Reporting a problem",
      "tours": [
        "whats-new-0.1.0-beta.1",
      ],
    },
    {
      "body": [
        "This is a beta: what it doesn't do yet, and what hasn't been tried in the game.",
        "",
        "**In your mod**",
        "",
        "- **A masculine V: not tried in the game yet.** Build makes XF Eye Artistry for both a feminine and a masculine V, but the masculine character creator's XF row hasn't been seen in the game yet.",
        "- **Shimmer and Glitter are waiting for a check in the game.** Both were reworked after they didn't look right in the game (Shimmer showed as glossy vinyl), and the new versions haven't been tried in the game yet. Until they pass, the finish picker offers them only with **Show research tools** on; a layer that already uses one keeps it, and Glitter isn't built into your mod.",
        "- **Some finishes are still experiments.** Glossy doesn't look different from Satin yet. A Colour-shifting look holds only one Colour-shifting layer. **Colours and finishes** says which finishes go into your mod.",
        "- **Full-face masks: not tried in the game yet.** An item that hides V's whole head should hide the makeup with it. An ordinary helmet covers the makeup, as it covers the game's own.",
        "- **Expression sets are checked by Build but not tried in photo mode yet.**",
        "",
        "If something doesn't work in the game, use **Report a problem…** at the bottom of Help.",
        "",
        "**In the 3D view**",
        "",
        "- **Finishes look closer to each other in the game.** Under the character creator's soft light they barely separate; the 3D view shows them further apart.",
        "- **Face movement: not checked against the game yet.** The idle's face, the blink and the live face in Expressions come from your game's own facial setup, but may not match the game exactly.",
        "- **Clothes from mods aren't drawn.** The 3D view dresses V in the game's own clothes from your save; clothes that mods add aren't shown yet.",
        "",
        "**Installing and updating**",
        "",
        "- **Updates are downloaded by hand.** XF Studio tells you when a newer version is out (it looks when it starts; **Settings › Updates** turns that off), and **Check for updates** in Help looks now. New versions are on the **Releases** page on GitHub. Export your looks before installing one.",
        "- **Windows may warn before the setup runs,** because the app isn't signed yet. Choose **More info**, then **Run anyway**.",
      ],
      "id": "limitations",
      "keywords": "limitations known problems missing not yet later version beta tried masculine male finish shimmer glitter research tools glossy colour-shifting mask helmet face blink expressions photo mode clothes mods updates releases windows warning signed smartscreen run anyway report",
      "title": "What's not in this version yet",
    },
    {
      "body": "Drag a panel's tab to dock it beside another, or onto a floating spot. The **Panels** button in the header opens or closes panels in the current tab. To reset a tab, open its menu (right-click the layout tab or press Shift+F10 while it's focused) and choose **Reset to default**. [[key:shell.regions]] moves the keyboard focus between regions.",
      "id": "layout",
      "keywords": "panel dock float tab layout reset move window",
      "title": "Panels and layout",
    },
  ],
  "tours": [
    {
      "audience": "onboarding",
      "id": "onboarding",
      "steps": [
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "layer.added",
          },
          "anchor": "layers.add",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "command": {
                    "kind": "add",
                  },
                  "kind": "layer.edit",
                },
                "kind": "studio",
              },
              "label": "Add a layer for me",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Each layer is one shape of makeup with its own colour and finish. Layers stack like real makeup: the top of the list sits in front.",
              "",
              "Start by adding a layer, or use one that's already there.",
            ],
            "title": "Looks are made of layers",
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "recipe.edited",
          },
          "anchor": "uv.canvas",
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "This flat map is where you shape the selected layer.",
              "",
              "- Drag a point to reshape it; drag inside the shape to move it.",
              "- Double-click the outline to add a point.",
              "- Hold **Shift** and drag to rotate, or Shift-wheel to scale.",
              "- The wheel zooms and right-drag pans. [[key:uv.fit]] fits the shape.",
              "",
              "Try moving a point. [[key:shell.undo]] takes any change back.",
            ],
            "title": "Draw on the UV map",
          },
          "placement": "auto",
        },
        {
          "anchor": "head.view",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "kind": "camera.front",
                },
                "kind": "studio",
              },
              "label": "Show the front view",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Your changes appear on the 3D head as you work. Drag to turn the view, use the wheel to zoom and right-drag to pan. [[key:head.front]] returns to the front view.",
              "",
              "If the 3D view isn't set up yet, this pane shows the one next step. The UV map works without it.",
            ],
            "title": "See it on V's head",
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "any": [
              {
                "event": "finish.changed",
              },
              {
                "event": "color.changed",
              },
            ],
          },
          "anchor": "finish.picker",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "finish": "metallic",
                  "kind": "layer.setFinish",
                },
                "kind": "studio.activeLayer",
              },
              "label": "Try Metallic",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "Pick the layer's colour, then its finish. Matte, Satin and Metallic go into your mod today; the picker groups the others by how far they can go.",
            "title": "Choose a colour and a finish",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "presets.list",
          "content": {
            "body": "A preset is one finished look. Each preset becomes one choice in the game's eye makeup selector, so a collection of presets is the set of looks you'll pick from in the character creator.",
            "title": "Presets are complete looks",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.save",
          "content": {
            "body": "Your work saves itself to the local library as you go, so closing the app never loses it. **Save version** ([[key:shell.save]]) keeps a version of your collection there, beside its earlier versions, that you can go back to.",
            "title": "Keep your work in the library",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.package",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "kind": "panel",
                "panel": "package",
              },
              "label": "Open Mod package",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "When your looks are ready, open **Mod package**.",
              "",
              "- **Check** lists which looks can become mod files, and names anything that would be left out and why. It needs no game files.",
              "- **Build** makes the mod files. **Add to my mod manager** adds them to your game when you choose to.",
            ],
            "title": "Make your mod",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.help",
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Open **Help** with [[key:shell.help]] for tours, answers and every keyboard and mouse shortcut. [[key:shell.palette]] finds any command by name.",
              "",
              "**Your first eye makeup mod**, in Help's Guided tours, takes you from two looks to a mod in your game.",
            ],
            "title": "Help is always here",
          },
        },
      ],
      "summary": "A two-minute look at layers, drawing, the 3D view, colour and finish, your library and making the mod.",
      "title": "Getting started",
    },
    {
      "audience": "howto",
      "id": "your-v-and-view",
      "steps": [
        {
          "anchor": "panel.character",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "kind": "savedV.import",
                },
                "kind": "file",
              },
              "label": "Load V from a save…",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "The **Character** panel holds your V's character-creator options, read from your game and mods.",
              "",
              "- Load a save to see your own V.",
              "- Change any option to try your looks on another face, and save a set of options as a preset.",
              "",
              "None of this changes your looks or your save.",
            ],
            "title": "Your V",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "panel.lighting",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "kind": "preview.selectLightingSetup",
                  "setup": "creator",
                },
                "kind": "studio",
              },
              "label": "Use creator lighting",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "**Camera & light** frames the view and lights your V. Choose a lighting setup, such as **Character creator** to compare with the game, or make your own and aim its lights with the direction dial.",
              "",
              "Camera and light never change your looks or your mod.",
            ],
            "title": "Camera & light",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.settings",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "kind": "panel",
                "panel": "settings",
              },
              "label": "Open Settings",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "**Settings** holds what XF Studio needs to know about your computer: your game folder, your mod manager, your saves and WolvenKit. XF Studio finds these for you; change one here if it guessed wrong.",
            "title": "Your game and mod manager",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.help",
          "content": {
            "body": "Open **Help** with [[key:shell.help]] for the other tours, answers for each part of the Studio, and **What's not in this version yet**.",
            "title": "Help is always here",
          },
        },
      ],
      "summary": "Where your V's creator options, the camera and lights, and your game and mod manager settings live.",
      "title": "Your V, camera and settings",
    },
    {
      "audience": "howto",
      "id": "first-eye-mod",
      "keywords": "first mod eye makeup make looks check build install add mod manager character creator walkthrough how to",
      "steps": [
        {
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "XF Studio is open in another window, so this one is read-only. This tour makes looks and a mod, so it needs the window that can make changes.",
              "",
              "Use that window, or choose **Use it here** at the top of this window to work here instead, then start the tour again from Help.",
            ],
            "title": "This window can't make changes",
          },
          "id": "read-only",
          "when": {
            "writable": false,
          },
        },
        {
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "In a few minutes you'll make **two eye makeup looks**, build them into your own **XF Eye Artistry** mod and add it to your game, ready to try in the character creator.",
              "",
              "Where a step is fiddly, **Do it for me** does it for you, Colour, finish and layer edits can be undone. Adding a preset works like **Add preset**: remove it from the Presets list if you no longer want it; the removal offers Restore. The two looks are added to the collection you have open; nothing you already made is changed.",
            ],
            "title": "Your first eye makeup mod",
          },
          "id": "intro",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "preset.added",
          },
          "anchor": "presets.add",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "command": {
                    "kind": "add",
                  },
                  "kind": "preset.edit",
                },
                "capture": "preset",
                "kind": "studio",
                "target": "first",
              },
              "label": "Do it for me",
              "then": "next",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "A **preset** is one complete look, and each one becomes a choice in the game. **Add preset** starts it with your default starter shape (**Lid wash**, a soft wash over the eyelid, until you choose another default).",
              "",
              "Press **Add preset**, or let me do it.",
            ],
            "title": "First look: add a preset",
          },
          "id": "first-look-add",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "finish.changed",
          },
          "anchor": "panel.finish",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "kind": "sequence",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "action": {
                      "color": "#a8576b",
                      "kind": "layer.setColor",
                    },
                    "kind": "studio.activeLayer",
                    "target": "first",
                  },
                  {
                    "action": {
                      "finish": "regular",
                      "kind": "layer.setFinish",
                    },
                    "kind": "studio.activeLayer",
                    "target": "first",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "label": "Do it for me",
              "then": "next",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "Choose the layer's colour, then its finish. Matte, Satin and Metallic go into your mod today. A rose colour with the Satin finish suits a first look.",
            "title": "First look: colour and finish",
          },
          "id": "first-look-style",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "preset.added",
          },
          "anchor": "presets.add",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "command": {
                    "kind": "add",
                  },
                  "kind": "preset.edit",
                },
                "capture": "preset",
                "kind": "studio",
                "target": "second",
              },
              "label": "Do it for me",
              "then": "next",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "Add a second preset for a different look. It starts with your default starter layer; the next step adds a second layer to it.",
            "title": "Second look: add another preset",
          },
          "id": "second-look-add",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "layer.added",
          },
          "anchor": "layers.starters",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "command": {
                    "kind": "add",
                    "starter": "classic-wing",
                  },
                  "kind": "layer.edit",
                },
                "capture": "layer",
                "kind": "studio",
                "target": "second",
              },
              "label": "Do it for me",
              "then": "next",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "A look can have several layers, like real makeup: a wash on the lid with a liner on top. Open the arrow beside **Add layer** and choose **Classic wing**, a clean liner with a flick past the outer corner.",
              "",
              "The other starter shapes are in the same menu.",
            ],
            "title": "Second look: a different starter shape",
          },
          "id": "second-look-shape",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "finish.changed",
          },
          "anchor": "panel.finish",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "kind": "sequence",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "action": {
                      "color": "#2c3a5e",
                      "kind": "layer.setColor",
                    },
                    "kind": "studio.activeLayer",
                    "target": "second",
                  },
                  {
                    "action": {
                      "finish": "metallic",
                      "kind": "layer.setFinish",
                    },
                    "kind": "studio.activeLayer",
                    "target": "second",
                  },
                ],
              },
              "label": "Do it for me",
              "then": "next",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "Give the new layer its own colour and finish. A deep blue with the Metallic finish stands well apart from the first look.",
            "title": "Second look: colour and finish",
          },
          "id": "second-look-style",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "package.checked",
          },
          "anchor": "package.check",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "kind": "package.check",
                },
                "kind": "file",
              },
              "label": "Check for me",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Open **Mod package** and press **Check**. It lists which looks can become mod files, and names anything it would leave out and why.",
              "",
              "Check creates no files and changes nothing.",
            ],
            "title": "Check your looks",
          },
          "id": "check",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "package.setup",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "kind": "settings",
                "section": "game",
              },
              "label": "Open Settings › Game",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "XF Studio needs to know where your game and mod manager are before it can build your mod. The **Game** card here says the one thing to do next, with a button where it can.",
              "",
              "**Settings › Game** holds the rest. Once the card says it's ready, this tour carries on by itself.",
            ],
            "title": "One thing first: your game and mod manager",
          },
          "id": "setup",
          "when": {
            "setup": "needs",
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "package.built",
          },
          "anchor": "package.build",
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Press **Build mod files** and confirm. Building can take a minute or two, and you can stop it with **Stop** beside the progress.",
              "",
              "Nothing goes into your game yet: Build only makes the mod files.",
            ],
            "title": "Build your mod",
          },
          "id": "build",
          "when": {
            "setup": "ready",
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "advanceWhen": {
            "event": "mod.installed",
          },
          "anchor": "package.install",
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Press **Add to my mod manager**. It shows exactly what will be added and where before anything changes. If you install mods by hand, **Show in folder** opens the built mod instead.",
              "",
              "Either way only the **XF Eye Artistry** mod is added: your other mods and frameworks are never changed.",
            ],
            "title": "Add it to your game",
          },
          "id": "install",
          "when": {
            "built": true,
            "setup": "ready",
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
        {
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "Start the game (through Mod Organizer 2, if you use it) and open the character creator.",
              "",
              "- Among the head options, near the eye makeup, there's a new row labelled **XF**. The mod itself is called XF Eye Artistry.",
              "- Its choices are **Off** and your two looks, named as in your Presets list.",
              "- Choose each look and check the eyes show the colour, shape and finish you made.",
              "",
              "If the row isn't there: [[help:install|Installing your mod]] in Help.",
              "",
              "The masculine V row is not yet game-tested.",
            ],
            "title": "What to check in the game",
          },
          "id": "in-game",
          "when": {
            "writable": true,
          },
        },
      ],
      "summary": "Make two eye makeup looks, build them into a mod and add it to your game, ready to try in the character creator.",
      "title": "Your first eye makeup mod",
    },
    {
      "audience": "whats-new",
      "id": "whats-new-0.1.0-beta.1",
      "steps": [
        {
          "anchor": "finish.picker",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "action": {
                  "finish": "metallic",
                  "kind": "layer.setFinish",
                },
                "kind": "studio.activeLayer",
              },
              "label": "Try Metallic",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "The finish picker now shows the finishes that go into your mod first. **Matte**, **Satin** and **Metallic** can go into your mod. **Glossy** and **Colour-shifting** can be built as experiments. **Shimmer** and **Glitter** are being reworked and wait for a check in the game, so the picker shows them only with **Show research tools** on (Settings › Appearance). A layer that already uses one keeps it.",
            "title": "Finishes that go into your mod",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "presets.list",
          "content": {
            "body": "**Add preset** now starts with a layer, like your first preset, so there's something to shape straight away. **Save as new collection** gives the copy its own name, and the Library panel lists your **Recent drafts** to bring any of them back.",
            "title": "New presets start ready",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.package",
          "buttons": [
            {
              "action": {
                "kind": "panel",
                "panel": "package",
              },
              "label": "Open Mod package",
            },
          ],
          "content": {
            "body": "**Build** makes your mod for a feminine and a masculine V: the masculine character creator gets its own row with the same looks. The masculine row hasn't been tried in the game yet; **What's not in this version yet** in Help lists what's still to check.",
            "title": "For a masculine V too",
          },
        },
        {
          "anchor": "header.help",
          "content": {
            "body": [
              "This is a beta, and your reports make it work on more setups. **Report a problem…** in Help prepares a report you review first; nothing is sent by itself. XF Studio tells you when a newer version is out; **Check for updates** in Help looks now.",
              "",
              "Every tour, including this one, is in **Help** ([[key:shell.help]]).",
            ],
            "title": "Tell us what doesn't work",
          },
        },
      ],
      "summary": "Finishes that go into your mod first, presets that start ready, a masculine V, and where to report a problem.",
      "title": "What's new in the beta",
      "version": "0.1.0-beta.1",
    },
  ],
